<< /A << /BBox [ 116.844 451.049 477.978 761.443 ] /O /Layout >> /Alt (Receiver operating characteristic curves compare three models for discrimination of respiratory distress syndrome. Model 1 includes HCA alone and has an AUC of 0.566. Model 2 includes gestational age and birth weight and has an AUC of 0.824. Model 3 additionally includes HCA and has an AUC of 0.829. Sensitivity is plotted against one minus specificity, with the diagonal reference line indicating chance-level discrimination. Shaded areas represent bootstrap 95% confidence bands. Models 2 and 3 show substantially better discrimination than HCA alone.) /K 8 /Lang (en-EN) /P 18 0 R /Pg 125 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
